# Local Execution Guidance

Local development commands are allowed when they stay within the project and help validate code changes.

Allowed by default:

- Python import checks, unit tests, linting, formatting, and type checks.
- CLI help commands and commands that operate only on local fixtures or local databases.
- Short one-off commands that validate behavior without contacting third-party systems.

Ask before running commands that:

- Fetch live jobs, crawl websites, or contact third-party APIs.
- Start long-running schedulers, watchers, servers, or browser automation.
- Install new dependencies or make broad environment changes.
- Write outside the local repository.

If validation is skipped because it would contact external systems or run for a long time, state what was not run and why.
